---
interface Props {scene: 'queue'|'constraint'|'runner'|'index'|'representation'; number:number;}
const {scene,number}=Astro.props;
const scenes={
 queue:{title:'A waiting DDL statement can queue later readers',choice:'DDL response',modes:['Leave waiting','Cancel the attempt'],labels:['Reader A','Schema session B','Later reader C'],steps:[
 ['A reads inside BEGIN','A holds ACCESS SHARE until its transaction ends. B and C have not arrived.',['Reading orders · lock held','Not submitted','Not submitted']],
 ['B requests a column','ACCESS EXCLUSIVE conflicts with A. B waits; it has not added a column.',['Transaction still open','Waiting behind A','Not submitted']],
 ['C asks to read','C would be compatible with A. The earlier conflicting request B puts C in the queue.',['Transaction still open','Waiting behind A','Waiting behind B']],
 ['Act on the waiting DDL','The operator owns cancellation of B. A remains open in both alternatives.',['Still holding its lock','B still waiting','C still waiting'],['Still holding its lock','Cancelled · 57014','Read completes']],
 ['End the attempt','Ending B’s failed explicit transaction restores its session. The column was never committed.',['A may finish normally','B needs ROLLBACK','C still queued'],['A may finish normally','ROLLBACK · ready to retry','C has its answer']],
 ]},
 constraint:{title:'Enforcement can begin before historical proof',choice:'Historical repair',modes:['Repair before validation','Leave the old violation'],labels:['Old order 1','New order 4','Catalogue evidence'],steps:[
 ['Before the rule','Order 1 already contains −1. No amount rule yet protects writes.',['amount = −1','−2 would be accepted','No check']],
 ['Add CHECK NOT VALID','Installation skips the historical scan. It still checks every new or updated row.',['−1 still present','INSERT −2 rejected','enforced true · validated false']],
 ['Try validation','The scan meets −1 and fails. Its failure does not remove the installed rule.',['−1 fails the scan','INSERT −2 still rejected','validated false']],
 ['Repair or leave it','An authorised correction changes the old value. Concurrent writes must keep satisfying the rule.',['amount = 100','INSERT 400 succeeds','Ready to validate'],['amount = −1','INSERT 400 succeeds','Old violation remains']],
 ['Validate again','Validation proves the entire existing set under continued enforcement.',['100 passes','400 passes','validated true'],['−1 fails again','400 passes','validated false · stop']],
 ]},
 runner:{title:'One history entry cannot cover every committed stage',choice:'Runner boundary',modes:['Default transaction','noTransaction()'],labels:['First statement','Later statement','After failure'],steps:[
 ['Start one migration','The runner holds its session advisory lock. An ordinary migration starts a transaction.',['ALTER adds a column','SELECT 1 / 0 follows','No new history yet'],['CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY','SELECT 1 / 0 follows','No new history yet']],
 ['First statement finishes','An uncommitted catalogue change and a separately committed index have different recovery paths.',['Column exists inside transaction','Not yet executed','Change is uncommitted'],['Index valid and committed','Not yet executed','Index already survives']],
 ['Later statement fails','Division by zero ends the migration before its success record.',['Column will roll back','22012 · failure','Runner rolls back'],['Index survives','22012 · failure','No history entry']],
 ['Inspect before retry','History alone looks the same in both cases. Inspect the object and definition as well.',['Column absent','Failure retained in log','Retry from unchanged stage'],['Index still valid','Failure retained in log','Inspect then repair/resume']],
 ]},
 index:{title:'A concurrent build has durable intermediate states',choice:'Failure case',modes:['Cancel before first scan','Duplicate key in scan'],labels:['Heap and writers','Index state','Next action'],steps:[
 ['Register the new index','The concurrent command runs outside a user transaction and commits an initial catalogue entry.',['Writes permitted','live · not ready · invalid','Observe phase and blockers']],
 ['Begin building','An older writer can delay progress. A scan of committed keys can instead reveal duplicates.',['Older writer remains open','Waiting · invalid','Cancel through owner'],['duplicate, duplicate, three','Scan finds duplicate','23505 · build fails']],
 ['Failure returns','The invalid object remains in these rehearsed cases. A name existing is not proof of completion.',['Writer later finishes','invalid · not ready','Inspect pg_index'],['Duplicate values remain','invalid · not ready','Inspect pg_index']],
 ['Clean up and correct','Drop the leftover separately. Fix the duplicate according to business meaning before another unique build.',['Drop invalid index','Name free again','Retry after blocker gate'],['Resolve duplicate; drop index','Name free again','Retry after data gate']],
 ['Complete and attach','The retry must finish its scans and waits. An eligible valid unique index can then become a constraint.',['Writes remain permitted','ready · valid; constraint owns it','Verify conindid and definition']],
 ]},
 representation:{title:'A rename follows identity, while readers need meaning',choice:'View switch',modes:['Replace the view deliberately','Only rename columns'],labels:['Stored order 2','View dependency','Read-switch gate'],steps:[
 ['Old representation','The original integer column is authoritative. The view points to that column’s identity.',['amount int = 200','View → old integer','Stay on old readers']],
 ['Add replacement','An added bigint column is empty for old rows. The schema alone establishes no conversion.',['amount = 200 · v2 = NULL','View → old integer','Do not switch']],
 ['Writers and backfill agree','The parent protocol and resumable job make matching v2 current. Checks and indexes are prepared separately.',['amount = 200 · v2 = 200','View → old integer','Reconcile under writer rule']],
 ['Rename under a short lock','Renaming amount to amount_old and v2 to amount preserves existing view dependencies.',['old int = 200 · amount bigint = 200','View → amount_old','Rename is insufficient']],
 ['Switch the consumer','Recreate this view with its chosen new output contract and verify application queries.',['old int = 200 · amount bigint = 200','New view → amount bigint','Checks pass; retain old path'],['old int = 200 · amount bigint = 200','Old view → amount_old','Stop: consumer still old']],
 ]},
};
const config=scenes[scene];
---
<figure class="schema-player" data-schema-player data-scene={scene} data-number={number} data-config={JSON.stringify(config)}>
 <figcaption><strong>Figure {number}. {config.title}</strong><span>Illustrative steps; no elapsed time or production workload is simulated.</span></figcaption>
 <label>{config.choice} <select data-mode>{config.modes.map((m,i)=><option value={i}>{m}</option>)}</select></label>
 <div class="schema-track" aria-hidden="true">{config.steps.map((s,i)=><span data-marker={i}>{i+1}</span>)}</div>
 <p class="schema-stage" data-title>{config.steps[0][0]}</p>
 <div class="schema-mechanism" data-mechanism></div>
 <div class="schema-lanes">{config.labels.map((label,i)=><div class="schema-lane"><strong>{label}</strong><p data-lane={i}>{config.steps[0][2][i]}</p></div>)}</div>
 <p data-explanation>{config.steps[0][1]}</p>
 <div class="schema-controls"><button type="button" data-prev aria-disabled="true">Previous</button><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-position aria-live="polite">Step 1 of {config.steps.length}</span></div>
</figure>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-schema-player]').forEach(root=>{
  if(root.dataset.ready)return;root.dataset.ready='yes';
  const cfg=JSON.parse(root.dataset.config!);let step=0,mode=0,playing=false,timer:ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>|undefined,visible=true;
  const get=(s:string)=>root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(s)!;
  function stop(){playing=false;clearTimeout(timer);get('[data-play]').textContent='Play';}
  function schedule(){clearTimeout(timer);if(!playing||!visible||document.hidden)return;
   // Budget every visible label, option, diagram value, caption and explanation.
   const words=(root.textContent!.match(/\S+/g)||[]).length;
   timer=setTimeout(()=>{if(step<cfg.steps.length-1){step++;render();schedule();}else stop();},Math.max(10000,words*320+1800));
  }
  function mechanism(){
   const scene=root.dataset.scene,id='a29-arrow-'+root.dataset.number;
   const box=(x:number,y:number,w:number,title:string,value:string,flag='')=>`<g class="${flag}"><rect x="${x}" y="${y}" width="${w}" height="60" rx="5"/><text x="${x+w/2}" y="${y+23}" text-anchor="middle">${title}</text><text x="${x+w/2}" y="${y+45}" text-anchor="middle" class="value">${value}</text></g>`;
   const arrow=(x:number,y:number,x2:number,y2:number,label:string)=>`<path d="M${x},${y} L${x2},${y2}" marker-end="url(#${id})"/><text x="${(x+x2)/2}" y="${(y+y2)/2-9}" text-anchor="middle">${label}</text>`;
   let shapes='',description='';
   if(scene==='queue'){
    const cancelled=mode===1&&step>=3;
    shapes=box(10,65,140,'A · reader','lock held','held')+box(190,65,140,'B · DDL',step===0?'not submitted':cancelled?'cancelled':'waiting',cancelled?'removed':step>0?'waiting':'')+box(370,65,140,'C · reader',step<2?'not submitted':cancelled?'read completes':'waiting',step>=2&&!cancelled?'waiting':'');
    if(step>=1&&!cancelled)shapes+=arrow(190,88,155,88,'');
    if(step>=2&&!cancelled)shapes+=arrow(370,88,335,88,'');
    description='Arrows point from a waiting request to its blocker. Cancelling B removes both waiting edges.';
    shapes+='<text x="260" y="35" text-anchor="middle">waiter → blocker</text>';
   }else if(scene==='constraint'){
    const repaired=step>=3&&mode===0,valid=step===4&&mode===0;
    shapes=box(10,75,140,'Stored order 1',repaired?'100':'−1',repaired?'good':'waiting')+box(195,75,130,'CHECK gate',step===0?'absent':'amount ≥ 0',step?'held':'')+box(370,75,140,'Incoming order','−2',step?'waiting':'');
    shapes+=arrow(370,105,330,105,'');
    shapes+=`<text x="260" y="175" text-anchor="middle">${step===0?'new −2 can enter': 'new −2 is rejected · old row still needs proof'}</text>`;
    if(valid)shapes+='<text x="80" y="52" text-anchor="middle">✓ historical proof</text>';
    description='The installed gate rejects the new negative amount even before the old amount has been repaired and validated.';
   }else if(scene==='runner'){
    const committed=mode===1&&step>=1;
    shapes=box(10,75,145,'First change',step===0?'submitted':committed?'committed':step<3?'uncommitted':'absent',committed?'held':'')+box(190,75,140,'Second statement',step<2?'not run':'1 ÷ 0 · error',step>=2?'waiting':'')+box(370,75,140,'History row','absent');
    shapes+=arrow(155,105,185,105,'')+arrow(330,105,365,105,'');
    shapes+=`<path class="boundary" d="M5,60 H${mode===0?'340':'160'} V148 H5 Z"/><text x="260" y="177" text-anchor="middle">${mode===0?'dashed boundary: rollback removes first change':'first commit survives the later failure'}</text>`;
    description='The transaction boundary determines whether the first change survives when the second statement fails.';
   }else if(scene==='index'){
    const done=step===4,clean=step===3;
    shapes=box(10,75,140,'Table keys',mode&&step<3?'dup · dup · three':'one · two · three')+box(195,75,130,'Index',clean?'removed':done?'VALID':'INVALID',done?'good':clean?'removed':'waiting')+box(370,75,140,'Constraint',done?'owns index':'absent',done?'held':'');
    if(!clean)shapes+=arrow(155,105,190,105,done?'built':'');
    if(done)shapes+=arrow(330,105,365,105,'');
    shapes+=`<text x="260" y="175" text-anchor="middle">${done?'valid index → short attachment → constraint':clean?'cleanup removes the incomplete object':'failure can leave an object without a usable read path'}</text>`;
    description='Table data, the separate index and its eventual constraint ownership are three different states.';
   }else{
    const renamed=step>=3,switched=step===4&&mode===0;
    shapes=box(10,100,145,renamed?'amount_old · int':'amount · int','200','held')+box(195,100,135,renamed?'amount · bigint':'amount_v2 · bigint',step===0?'absent':step===1?'NULL':'200',step>=2?'good':'')+box(370,10,140,'Existing reader',switched?'new view':'old view');
    shapes+=arrow(440,70,switched?265:82,95,switched?'new dependency':'original dependency');
    if(step>=2)shapes+=arrow(160,140,190,140,'');
    shapes+='<text x="260" y="185" text-anchor="middle">Renaming labels does not retarget an existing dependency.</text>';
    description='The reader pointer stays attached to the old integer column through renaming; deliberate view replacement points it to bigint.';
   }
   get('[data-mechanism]').innerHTML=`<svg viewBox="0 0 520 200" role="img" aria-label="${description}"><defs><marker id="${id}" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 Z"/></marker></defs>${shapes}</svg>`;
  }
  function render(){mechanism();const item=cfg.steps[step],values=mode&&item[3]?item[3]:item[2];
   get('[data-title]').textContent=item[0];get('[data-explanation]').textContent=item[1];
   values.forEach((v:string,i:number)=>get(`[data-lane="${i}"]`).textContent=v);
   root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-marker]').forEach((m,i)=>{m.dataset.current=String(i===step);m.dataset.past=String(i<step);});
   get('[data-position]').textContent=`Step ${step+1} of ${cfg.steps.length}`;
   get('[data-prev]').setAttribute('aria-disabled',String(step===0));get('[data-next]').setAttribute('aria-disabled',String(step===cfg.steps.length-1));
  }
  get('[data-prev]').onclick=()=>{stop();step=Math.max(0,step-1);render();};
  get('[data-next]').onclick=()=>{stop();step=Math.min(cfg.steps.length-1,step+1);render();};
  get('[data-reset]').onclick=()=>{stop();step=0;render();};
  get('[data-play]').onclick=()=>{if(playing){stop();return;}if(step===cfg.steps.length-1)step=0;playing=true;get('[data-play]').textContent='Pause';render();schedule();};
  get('[data-mode]').onchange=e=>{mode=Number((e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value);render();schedule();};
  new IntersectionObserver(entries=>{visible=entries[0].isIntersecting;if(visible)schedule();else clearTimeout(timer);}).observe(root);
  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange',()=>{if(document.hidden)clearTimeout(timer);else schedule();});render();
 });
</script>
<style>
 .schema-player{border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:.6rem;padding:1rem;margin:1.8rem 0;background:var(--color-surface)}
 figcaption{margin:0 0 1rem}figcaption span{display:block;font-size:.82rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-top:.3rem}
 label{display:flex;gap:.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;font-size:.85rem}select,button{font:inherit;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:.25rem;padding:.45rem .6rem}
 .schema-track{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:.3rem;margin:1rem 0}.schema-track span{border:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:.25rem .6rem;border-radius:1rem;font: .8rem var(--font-mono)}
 .schema-track span[data-current="true"]{background:var(--color-text);color:var(--color-surface)}.schema-track span[data-past="true"]{border-width:2px}
 .schema-mechanism{margin:.7rem 0;overflow:hidden}.schema-mechanism :global(svg){width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.schema-mechanism :global(rect){fill:var(--color-surface-alt);stroke:var(--color-rule);stroke-width:1.5}.schema-mechanism :global(text){font:12px var(--font-mono);fill:var(--color-text)}.schema-mechanism :global(.value){font-weight:700}.schema-mechanism :global(path){fill:none;stroke:var(--color-text-secondary);stroke-width:1.5}.schema-mechanism :global(marker path){fill:var(--color-text);stroke:none}.schema-mechanism :global(.held rect){stroke:var(--color-text);stroke-width:3}.schema-mechanism :global(.waiting rect){stroke-dasharray:5 3;stroke:var(--color-text)}.schema-mechanism :global(.removed){opacity:.5}.schema-mechanism :global(.good rect){stroke:var(--color-text);stroke-width:3}.schema-mechanism :global(.boundary){stroke-dasharray:6 4}
 .schema-stage{font-weight:700}.schema-lanes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.6rem}.schema-lane{border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-left:4px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.7rem;font-size:.85rem;min-width:0}.schema-lane p{margin:.5rem 0 0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;min-height:4em}.schema-lane strong{font-size:.8rem}.schema-controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;font-size:.82rem}.schema-controls span{margin-left:auto}button[aria-disabled="true"]{opacity:.55}button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-text);outline-offset:3px}
 @media(max-width:600px){.schema-player{padding:.7rem}.schema-lanes{grid-template-columns:1fr}.schema-lane{display:grid;grid-template-columns:6.8rem 1fr;gap:.5rem;padding:.6rem}.schema-lane p{margin:0;min-height:2.5em}.schema-controls span{width:100%;margin:0}}
</style>
